A||N||3||Ferraro300zx||V6 running ROUGH and smoking. HELP||||11||
Z||000000||Ferraro300zx||11-06-2000||11:20 PM||||Hi, my dad just got this 328GTB kit car (85 fiero with 2.5 v6). Anyways, it was running good for a month when one day he tried to start it and it was missing really bad and the check engine light came on. It had a code for the MAP sensor, and the PROM. After I cleared the code, it ran fine for a few weeks. Two days ago, he drove it and it was running fine, parked it then he started it and it ran like crap, it wouldn't idle (sounds like it's only running on 2 cylinders), and fuel smoke was pouring out.<P>Has anyone had this problem before? I think it may be the PROM, but maybe someone can tell me otherwise? Thanx<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||StuGood||11-07-2000||01:01 AM||||I've never had a PROM error code, so I have no experience with that one.  But the first thing I'd probably try is changing the ignition module in the distributor.<P>BTW, if it's an original Fiero V6, it's a 2.8, rather than 2.5.  But you knew that.  Everyone makes typoze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyro86SE||11-07-2000||01:29 AM||||try changing the tps sensor and the fuel filter it might be starving for gas also you might want to check the egr valve i had similar problems not quite the same but close <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spryologo_1_1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||11-07-2000||04:37 PM||||That happened to me once in my '84.<P>I had just washed the engine and went to see if it would start. It ran like crap and was pouring out black smoke. I let it run for a minute and the problem fixed itself.<P>I know it doesn't help, just trying to relate. My car also had problems with the IAC valve so you might want to check that too.||||reg||1
